{\pard\sa120 SUPERIOR COURT OF WASHINGTON FOR KING COUNTY\par}
{\pard\sa120 {\b In re: MARISOL ECHEVARR\u205?A-LUND, Petitioner, and TREVOR J. LUND, Respondent.}\par}
{\pard\sa120 No. 26-2-11847-3 KNT\par}
{\pard\sb240\sa120\b\fs30 DECLARATION OF PETITIONER IN SUPPORT OF PETITION FOR PROTECTION ORDER (RCW 7.105.100)\par}
{\pard\sa120 {\b DRAFT - prepared with Eastside Legal Aid Clinic, advocate Dawn Okimoto, 6/22/2026. Petitioner's residential address is confidential under GR 22 and must not appear in the filed version.}\par}
{\pard\sa120 I, Marisol Echevarr\u237?a-Lund, declare as follows:\par}
{\pard\sa120 1. I am the Petitioner. I am 34 years old. My date of birth is October 5, 1991. Respondent, Trevor J. Lund, is my husband. His date of birth is 2/11/1987. We married in 2018 and separated on May 2, 2026. We have one child together, Paloma, who is six years old and in kindergarten at Little Cedars Montessori.\par}
{\pard\sa120 2. I am asking for protection for myself and for Paloma. Since May 2 I have been staying with my sister, Ines Echevarr\u237?a, in Kent. Before that we lived together at 23418 114th Place SE, Renton, WA 98031. Trevor still lives there.\par}
{\pard\sa120 3. {\b Most recent incident.} On the night of Friday, June 12, 2026, Trevor came to Ines's apartment at about 11:15 p.m. He pounded on the door and yelled that he would "burn the place down" if I did not bring Paloma out. He was driving his gray pickup, Washington plate C81 447K. Ines's neighbor, Reggie Tate, saw him and called 911. Kent Police responded (incident no. 26-0041877) but Trevor had left.\par}
{\pard\sa120 4. {\b Text messages.} Between June 12 and June 19, 2026 Trevor sent me 141 text messages from his number, (425) 555-0155, and from a second number I did not recognize, 206.555.0108. Screenshots are attached as Exhibit A. They include: "you cant hide at ines place forever," "I know what time you get off," and a photo of the front door of my work.\par}
{\pard\sa120 5. {\b Physical violence.} On April 18, 2026, during an argument about money, Trevor grabbed my left arm and twisted it behind my back. I was treated the next morning at Harborview Urgent Care - Renton for a fractured left wrist (visit no. UC-3391047). I told the provider I had fallen. That was not true. I was afraid of what he would do if he was arrested. Records are attached as Exhibit B. I was eleven weeks pregnant at the time; I miscarried on April 30.\par}
{\pard\sa120 6. {\b Firearms.} Trevor owns at least two firearms: a 9mm handgun, serial number BFKR447, which he keeps in the truck console, and a hunting rifle. In March he placed the handgun on the kitchen table during an argument and said, "This is how it ends."\par}
{\pard\sa120 7. {\b Substance use and history.} Trevor has used methamphetamine on and off since 2023. He has a 2021 conviction for assault in the fourth degree involving a former girlfriend in Pierce County. He lost his job as a longshoreman in January and blames me.\par}
{\pard\sa120 8. {\b Surveillance.} On June 15 I found a tracking device taped under the rear bumper of my car, a blue 2015 hatchback, plate BXT9920. The device ID printed on it is TG-88-41C7-0093. Trevor also knows the passcode to my phone (0513, Paloma's birthday) and my email password. I have since changed both.\par}
{\pard\sa120 9. {\b My work.} I am a dental hygienist at Cascade Family Dental, 410 Rainier Avenue South, Suite B, Renton. Trevor has come to the parking lot twice since we separated. I ask that he be ordered to stay 1,000 feet away from my work, from Ines's home, and from Paloma's school.\par}
{\pard\sa120 10. {\b Immigration.} Trevor has told me many times that he will "call immigration" on me and on my mother. I am a lawful permanent resident; my card number is A-204-417-883. My mother has a pending asylum case. I am afraid for her.\par}
{\pard\sa120 11. I can be reached through my advocate, Ms. Okimoto, at 206-555-0170 ext. 12 or dokimoto@eastsidelegalaid.example. Please do not send mail to the Renton house.\par}
{\pard\sa120 I declare under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of Washington (RCW 9A.72.085) that the foregoing is true and correct.\par}
